No key material in logs (m150 rebase of no-key-log.patch) + no ICE password.

1) FrameCryptor. Upstream webrtc-sdk/webrtc m150_release still prints, at
RTC_LOG(LS_INFO), the input secret, the salt and the DERIVED AES key as
decimal byte lists every time a frame-cryptor key is installed
(DeriveHkdfSha256FromSecret, frame_crypto_transformer.cc:264;
DerivePBKDF2KeyFromRawKey, :288). m150 changed the helper call to
to_uint8_list(<vector>) (m144 was to_uint8_list(ptr, len)), so the m144
no-key-log.patch no longer applies. Both statements are deleted with no
replacement log line. to_uint8_list() stays (external linkage, now unused ->
no -Wunused-function). The positive control of the binary gate
("Failed to derive HkdfSha256 key from secret.", :260) is untouched.

2) ICE. p2p/base/port.cc (Port::GetStunMessage, :519 and :586) prints the
local ICE password (password_) at LS_ERROR whenever a STUN request with a bad
MESSAGE-INTEGRITY arrives - an unauthenticated remote packet can therefore
make every default log capture record the ICE credential. Only the
", password_=" field is removed; the rest of the error line stays.

Binary gate: ci/assert-no-key-strings.sh (derived_key / "slat << " / raw_key)
must find 0 hits; m150 builds also pass -F 'password_=' (see that script).

Order: after P1 and P2 (m150/apply-series.sh: P1, P2, P3, ...). Hunks do not
overlap with P1/P2. Verified: `git apply --check` clean alone and after
P1 + P2 against webrtc-sdk/webrtc @ ba469aa2093ba950066258ca0a59a6fbd1295582
(frame_crypto_transformer.cc blob 1b4b4def08b5, port.cc blob 641d1e32348e).

diff --git a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
index 1b4b4de..a7fb722 100644
--- a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
+++ b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
@@ -261,12 +261,11 @@ int DeriveHkdfSha256FromSecret(const std::vector<uint8_t>& secret,
     return ErrorUnexpected;
   }
 
-  RTC_LOG(LS_INFO) << "secret " << to_uint8_list(secret)
-                   << " len " << secret.size() << " slat << "
-                   << to_uint8_list(salt) << " len "
-                   << salt.size() << "\n derived_key "
-                   << to_uint8_list(derived_key)
-                   << " len " << derived_key.size();
+  // SECURITY: never log key material. Upstream printed the input secret, the
+  // salt and the derived key here as decimal byte lists at LS_INFO; apps that
+  // enable INFO logging (RTCSetMinDebugLogLevel(.info), logcat, ...) then leak
+  // the E2EE frame key into their log capture and any uploaded diagnostics.
+  // Removed; keep it removed when rebasing on upstream.
 
   return Success;
 }
@@ -285,13 +284,8 @@ int DerivePBKDF2KeyFromRawKey(const std::vector<uint8_t> raw_key,
     return ErrorUnexpected;
   }
 
-  RTC_LOG(LS_INFO) << "raw_key "
-                   << to_uint8_list(raw_key) << " len "
-                   << raw_key.size() << " slat << "
-                   << to_uint8_list(salt) << " len "
-                   << salt.size() << "\n derived_key "
-                   << to_uint8_list(derived_key)
-                   << " len " << derived_key.size();
+  // SECURITY: never log key material (raw key, salt, derived key). See the
+  // note in DeriveHkdfSha256FromSecret().
 
   return Success;
 }
